<problem>
  <title>Solving and Classifying a 2×2 Linear System</title>

  <p>Consider the following system of linear equations:</p>
  <md>
    <mrow>2x + 3y = 0</mrow>
    <mrow>4x - y = 14</mrow>
  </md>

  <part>
    <p>Find the solution to the system.</p>
    <p>
      <m>x = </m><mathInput name="userX"/>, 
      <m>y = </m><mathInput name="userY"/>
    </p>
    <answer name="solAns">
      <award>
        <when>$userX = 3 and $userY = -2</when>
      </award>
    </answer>

    <hint>
      <p>
        Try eliminating <m>y</m> by multiplying the second equation by <m>3</m> and adding it to the first equation.
      </p>
    </hint>
  </part>

  <part>
    <p>Based on its solution set, how is this system classified?</p>
    <answer name="classAns">
      <choice credit="1">Consistent and independent</choice>
      <choice>Consistent and dependent</choice>
      <choice>Inconsistent</choice>
    </answer>
  </part>
</problem>
